findings.what:
The brief names distinct materials: linen, felt tabard, leather, ash wood and glossy dawnglass. In every close view they read as smooth painted clay:
- the sleeves are uniform pale cylinders;
- the straps are dark tubes with no edge or stitching;
- the bow has no grain or worn bevel;
- the visor and caps have no reflection.

The cause is the albedo painting, not texture resolution. Peers in the same renderer and texture budget carry painted plates, trims, scale patterns and fold shading; Lisvel's albedo islands are mostly flat tone fills.

findings.fix:
Paint the materials in the 2048 albedo through the procedural painters:
- ash limbs: grain along the limb, growth lines near the grip, pale worn bevels;
- linen: fold shadows gathering into the bracers and a 2-3 % weave breakup;
- leather: a lit top edge, stitched border and scuffs where the quiver rubs;
- felt tabard: a nap and a darker hem;
- dawnglass: a painted horizon reflection and a lower roughness on the accent/glass parts.

Baking normal and ORM at 1024 is optional and secondary.
